From: fil-c-utils maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Use portable sntrup cryptoint on Fil-C AArch64

Fil-C 0.683 supports safe inline assembly only on x86-64. The generated
cryptoint code otherwise selects its AArch64 assembly because Fil-C presents
the normal GNU-compatible target macros, leaving sntrup761x25519 key exchange
to panic when it reaches the first instruction.

Exclude only Fil-C from the generated AArch64 conditions so it selects
cryptoint's existing portable C fallbacks. Preserve the x86-64 assembly and all
non-Fil-C behavior. Apply the same deterministic transform in the import script
so regenerating sntrup761.c retains the compatibility rule. The portable code
uses cryptoint's volatile blockers to resist timing-changing optimization, but
the resulting Fil-C AArch64 machine code is not claimed to be constant-time.

--- a/sntrup761.sh
+++ b/sntrup761.sh
@@ -48,2 +48,5 @@
-	#  - remove unnecessary defines and externs.
-	sed -e "/#include/d" \
+	#  - remove unnecessary defines and externs.
+	#  - use portable cryptoint on Fil-C AArch64: Fil-C 0.683 cannot lower
+	#    AArch64 inline assembly.
+	sed -e "/#include/d" \
+	    -e '/^#elif defined(__GNUC__) && defined(__aarch64__)$/s/$/ \&\& !defined(__FILC__)/' \
